{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "NestJS Backend Foundation Starter",
    "description": "Manual-test collection for the NestJS Backend Foundation Starter public HTTP API.\n\nOpenAPI remains the canonical machine contract (`/v1/docs-json`). This collection must stay aligned with controllers and generated OpenAPI.\n\n## Dual auth drivers\n\n- **JWT (`AUTH_DRIVER=jwt`):** protected routes use `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}`. Refresh and logout send `{{refreshToken}}` in the JSON body.\n- **Session (`AUTH_DRIVER=session`):** protected routes and all `/v1/sessions/*` use Cookie `{{sessionCookieName}}={{sessionCookieValue}}` (default name `sid`). Under JWT, session routes return `400 SESSION_DRIVER_REQUIRED`.\n\nPaste tokens or cookie values into collection/environment variables before calling protected requests. Do not commit real secrets.\n\nHealth routes are version-neutral (no `/v1` prefix). Auth, Google Auth, and Sessions use the `/v1` global prefix.\n\nGoogle OAuth start/callback are browser redirect flows; the requests are included for inventory completeness.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
